==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
[[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Slime Cat]], as it would in any peon-heavy stage, works amazingly here, especially since there are Zombie enemies that it can use to launch its devastating waves. Alternatively, units with high pierce such as [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]], [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]], and [[Talents|Talented]] [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] can be used to clear out the peons if one does not own Slime.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
The main difference in this chapter is the addition of Zang Roos and UltraBaaBaas.

The Zang Roos are the main threat of the stage because they will burrow past your frontline and damage your base. This makes it very important to control which cats you send out as you will not be able to kill the Zang Roo if the cat limit is reached. [[Wushu Cat (Rare Cat)|Shigong Cat]] works extremely well here as he is [[Resistant]] to Zombies and can easily stall the Zang Roos with Research Combos.

If you bring a Barrier Breaker such as [[Fencer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kitty of Liberty]], then the UltraBaaBaas will not be an issue.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
The primary threats here are [[Sir Rel]] and [[Li'l Zyclone]]. [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]] is your best bet at handling the latter, and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] can deal with the former. Aside from these two, a fairly standard setup of mixed anti-Alien and anti-Zombie should work well. Your [[Cat Cannon]] should always be Holy Blast.

